\par\par \b \uc2  Europe says Russia must go it alone. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robert Mahoney \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 18:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BONN, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Major European powers told Russia on Wednesday it would have to go it alone in salvaging its battered economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Russia must do it by itself," said German Finance Theo Waigel. \par \par \uc2  He said neither the Group of Seven industrialised nations, the International Monetary Fund nor the European Union could fix Russia's problems. \par \par \uc2  French President Jacques Chirac urged Moscow to push through economic reforms, saying international support would only work if reforms were implemented decisively by the new government of acting prime minister Viktor Chernomyrdin. \par \par \uc2  A Berlin newspaper reported that German and French finance ministers planned to write to Russia urging "fundamental and possibly painful" reforms to fight Moscow's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt crisis. \par \par \uc2  The Berliner Tagesspiegel said in an unsourced report to appear on Thursday that Waigel had spoken by telephone with his French counterpart Dominique Strauss-Kahn on Monday and agreed to draft a joint letter. \par \par \uc2  Details are expected to be finalised by the end of the week, and the two will probably address the letter to Chernomyrdin, the paper said. \par \par \uc2  German finance officials were not immediately available to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  The British Treasury said it was closely monitoring the Russia crisis and was in contact with other Group of Seven members. \par \par \uc2  European sources said the four European members of the G7 - Germany, France, Britain and Italy-were in close contact but it was premature to speculate on a joint initiative or letter. \par \par \uc2  Waigel told reporters in Cologne it was up to the Russian government and Duma lower house of parliament to take action to restore confidence in the rouble. \par \par \uc2  He was speaking as the rouble plunged more than 40 percent against the German mark and a bewildered Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it could no longer afford to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The German government has ruled out granting any more international financial aid to Russia, on top of a $22.6 billion package put together by the IMF last month, until Russia implements agreed tax and budget reforms. \par \par \uc2  Germany is Russia's biggest foreign lender and investor. Russia's sovereign and commercial debt to Germany totals 75.8 billion marks. \par \par \uc2  The financial crisis led to declines in European shares. Frankfurt was hardest hit among major European bourses, with the Xetra-DAX plunging more than three percent in a reflection of German banks' estimated $30 billion exposure to Russian debt. \par \par \uc2  Waigel said Germany had good relations with Chernomyrdin, who was unexpectedly re-appointed by President Boris Yeltsin last weekend. \par \par \uc2  "We will make use of these relations to help Russia," Waigel added. \par \par \uc2  Chirac also offered moral support to Russia but insisted on reform. \par \par \uc2  In an annual speech to French ambassadors in Paris, Chirac said the international community should back efforts by IMF chief Michel Camdessus to ease the crisis. \par \par \uc2  But he added: "His \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the full support of the G7, will only succeeed if the essential domestic reforms sought by President Yeltsin are implemented resolutely by the new government of Chernomyrdin." \par \par \uc2  Chernomyrdin flew off to Ukraine suddenly on Wednesday to meet Camdessus. \par \par \uc2  Chirac renewed a call for a strengthening of the IMF, in particular by giving its policy-making interim committee decision-making powers. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01ldh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
