\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP:Russia Seen Close Imposing Ruble Exchange Controls \b0\par\par\uc2  By Leos Rousek \par \uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 18:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian government appeared close to imposing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls Wednesday as the ruble tumbled and long lines appeared at exchange booths throughout Moscow. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  canceled trading at the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICE) when it was overwhelmed by demand for dollars. Investors responded by snatching up other foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Deutsche marks. At the MICE, the ruble plummeted to RUR7.6 per mark from RUR4.4995 Tuesday. That implied the ruble had fallen to RUR13 per dollar, compared to RUR7.6 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  later announced that it would avoid massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conserve \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Those queuing at exchange booths had a hard time finding dollars to buy at any price. \par \par \uc2  "There are essentially no dollars available," said Eric Jayaweera, analyst at MFK Renaissance investment bank. "People can't even buy (the dollars) at exchange booths on the street and the black market is developing very quickly." \par \par \uc2  He estimated the running black market rate could be around RUR15 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  A Deutsche Bank economist estimated ruble cash and bank deposits total an equivalent of $50 billion. If even a portion of that were to be converted into dollars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves could be wiped out. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have the means to meet even 20% (of the outflow) if it were to go," said Marcel Cassard, chief economist at Deutsche Bank in London. "If locals continue to worry, there are going to be outflows. The only way to stop it is to impose controls." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1618GMT \par \par \uc2  1144 4220 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8q07aqk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
