\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concerns For Dlr/Yen On Back Burner For Now \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 20:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Heightened concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar/yen aren't being given much credence yet, even as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the week by staging a slight comeback Monday. \par \par \uc2  While much of the spotlight Monday focused on Russia and the fallout of its de facto ruble devaluation, the yen won't be overshadowed for long, as market participants eye dollar/yen levels on the top and bottom that could compel a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stole the show when it cut the lower limit for the ruble by 34% to RUR9.50, from RUR6.30, spurring discussions of what's next for the gravely ill Russian economy and what the devaluation means for other emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  "That's all we've been talking about this morning," said Bob Johnson, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN-AMRO Bank in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  However, the market managed to absorb the news in an orderly fashion after the dollar initially spiked higher against the yen and Deutsche mark early in Monday trading before retreating gradually for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  "In a sense the Russia story has played itself out," said Jamie Coleman, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Thomson Global Markets in Boston. \par \par \uc2  While further Russia-related developments may keep \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders preoccupied, they weren't ignoring renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings out of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Monday that the yen's depreciation is about to stop and the right time for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be effective is approaching. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1854GMT \par \par \uc2  1143 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8h06y4b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
