\par\par \b \uc2  =World Mkt Turmoil At A Glance:DJIA Up On Relief Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 17:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- U.S. equities have gotten out to a strong start in\par Friday's early trading, as a relief rally takes hold of the\par market. Banking stocks have rallied, as world market\par conditions ameliorated some concerns about the group's\par exposure to poor performing emerging economies, and on\par takeover talk centering on J.P. Morgan. The Dow Jones\par Industrial Average is up 50 points at 8509\par .\par    -- Russian stocks rebounded strongly Friday, boosted by\par heavy short-covering and hopes for another international\par bailout of Russia's finances. The Russian Trading System\par Index rose 14% to close at 115.00 points Friday, from 101.17\par points at the close of trading Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- The Russian ruble (RUR) closed lower\par Friday amid an almost complete paralysis on the interbank\par market, as mistrust between banks continued to reign. The\par dollar was fixed at RUR6.3100, down from RUR6.321, thanks to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said\par .\par    -- Russian President Boris Yeltsin said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't\par devalue the ruble.\par    -- A hunt for quality stocks helped U.K. blue-chips\par extended their early lead in midday trading as investors\par gained confidence from word Hong Kong authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to support their equity market. At 1157 GMT, the FTSE 100\par index of leading shares was up 110.6 points at 5510.1\par    -- Chemical stocks continue to buoy the German stock\par market at midafternoon, amid very thin trading volume that\par could signal a short-lived recovery after a turbulent week\par on the Frankfurt stock exchange, dealers said. At 1145 GMT,\par the key electronic Xetra DAX index was up 120.84 points, or\par 2.3%\par    -- Mexican stocks opened higher,\par bolstered by strength in Asian and Russian equities. The key\par IPC index was up 47.71 points, or 1.3%, to 3628.26\par July U.S. producer price index number.\par    -- Around 1435 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DEM1.7965, up\par from DEM1.7893 in London around 1241 GMT and up from\par DEM1.7835 in New York late Thursday. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par also changing hands at Y145.34, up from Y144.82 earlier in\par London and up from Y144.88 late Thursday in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-14-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1109EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4223 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8e01y3a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
