\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty hits all-time high on Russia despite c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Pawel Kozlowski \par \uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1998\par 16:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 14 (Reuters) - The zloty flew to a new all-time high despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it as foreigners rushed for Polish treasuries after \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  secured a huge aid deal which may help it overcome financial problems. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended at 8.41/8.34 percent firmer than the parity rate on Tuesday against Monday's 8.33/8.27 percent close as an estimated $200 million worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it down from intraday highs of more than 8.60 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the wave of optimism spilling out from Russia was coupled by expectations that Polish interest rates and the zloty's crawling devaluation could be cut on Thursday, when the Monetary Policy Council (RPP) meets. \par \par \uc2  "The market is generally expecting cuts in interest rates, by about 100 basis points, and zloty crawling peg by 0.1 point, which should be roughly neutral to the zloty," said Krzysztof Rybinski, chief economist at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "Apart from that, there is this pressure from foreigners who again perceive Poland as a very attractive emerging market after Russia stabilised. The situation is likely to continue, prompting more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Rybinski added. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on the local market, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 11, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded between 8.63 and 8.28 percent stronger than the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) add to the pressure for a cut in interest rates, with the zloty so strong and the situation in Russia looking to improve a little bit," said Ehsun Khan, analyst at Morgan Stanley & Co International in London. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already has many reasons to cut interest rates, but the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the likelihood that the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain in the absence of cuts just adds to the logic for a cut," Khan added. \par \par \uc2  Polish debt yields continued their steady slide on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Two-year notes were on Tuesday at 17.6/17.4 percent against the 18.49 percent average yield at the last auction on July 1. Five-year paper traded at 15.5/15.4 against 15.72 percent. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 52-week bill yield fell to 17.8/17.6 percent on Tuesday against an average of 18.2 percent at this Monday's primary auction. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7e00x25\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
