\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty/Russia -2: Polish Fundamentals Improved \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1998\par 18:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Concerns about Poland's current-account deficit have eased as export performance has been stronger than expected. A number of economists have reduced their forecast for the deficit at the end of the year to 3.5% of gross domestic product from 4% or more. \par \par \uc2  And the year-on-year inflation rate in May fell to 13.3% from 13.7% in April. \par \par \uc2  But a stronger zloty also increases the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the zloty approaches the limit of its 20-point trading band against a basket of western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "They will definitely have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty gets stronger," said Krzysztof Rybinski, chief economist at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Before the latest crisis in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the zloty within its trading band. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials privately have said they were relieved that the Russian crisis had taken the pressure off the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must once again deal with the strong zloty. \par \par \uc2  Even before Monday's accord between the international lenders and Russia was announced, analysts had predicted that the Polish monetary policy council, which meets on Thursday, would reduce key interest rates and lower the monthly devaluation rate of the zloty. \par \par \uc2  Many economists are forecasting that interest rates will likely be cut by one percentage point. Currently, the Lombard rate stands at 26%, and the rediscount rate is at 23.5%. Many also predict that the monthly devaluation rate will be reduced to 0.6% from 0.8%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-07-98 \par \par \uc2  1658GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7d05ydj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
