\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ruble Dn Vs Dlr, GKOs Also Dn; Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1998\par 16:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble (RUR) sank against the dollar in active trading Thursday, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Treasuries also weakened sharply on the back of heavy foreign selling, with traders blaming poor results at the government's weekly treasury auction Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the benchmark one-year treasury rose to 61.5% from 56% Tuesday. Yields on many other issues surged above 60%, which is where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set its refinancing rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar for next-day delivery closed at RUR6.2200-RUR6.2300, up from RUR6.2180-RUR6.2200 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The selling really started yesterday because there was no real support during the auction," said Pavel Patyako, trader at Chase Manhattan in Moscow. "In spite of the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to keep things together with the high (overnight) interest rates (Thursday), there was still a high demand for dollars." \par \par \uc2  Traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent several hundred million dollars in reserves defending the ruble Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They said the ruble weakened outside the daily official trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market, at 6.2220 rubles to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were few new developments within Russia to spark the selling. Investors fear an International Monetary Fund aid package for Russian markets is not coming soon enough to stave collapse, and many have been selling on fears of a devaluation of the ruble. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 25-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1444GMT \par \par \uc2  1150 1855 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6p05ff9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
