\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging debt prices bolstered by yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 23:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 17 (Reuters) - Emerging debt was up for the second straight day Wednesday as investors took heart, at least temporarily, from news that help is on the way for the troubled yen. \par \par \uc2  "The real catalyst for the rally was the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the dollar/yen," one emerging debt trader said. \par \par \uc2  The United States rode to the rescue of the battered Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in a dramatic shift from its recent hands-off approach on mounting concern about Japan's slumping economy. \par \par \uc2  Joining forces with Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Treasury Department instructed the New York Federal Reserve to spend an estimated $2 billion to boost the value of the yen against the dollar - the first U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen in more than six years. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  happens when central banks buy or sell a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open market to affect its value. \par \par \uc2  The value of the yen immediately surged to 137 to the dollar, compared with 142 yen just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen to its lowest level in eight years recently on fears the ailing Japanese economy would spark another round of Asian financial shocks. \par \par \uc2  The emerging debt market was bolstered also by rumours that an aid package from the Group of Seven Industrialised Nations (G-7) is on the way. \par \par \uc2  Moscow cancelled two of three government debt auctions that had been expected Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "This brought a feeling that Russia may have money very soon from other sources," an emerging debt trader said. \par \par \uc2  "I'd say 75 percent of the gains in Brady bond prices today came from the dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 25 percent came from \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  A top Russian finance official said Wednesday the country was considering launching at least one dollar-denominated Eurobond by the end of June. \par \par \uc2  And rumours circulated on Wall Street that Russia was seeking a 30-year, $1 billion issue, with a spread of around 775 basis points over U.S. Treasuries. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The benchmark Brazil C bond\tab \tab   was up 1-1/4 to bid 76-7/8, Argentine PARs\tab \tab  were up 1/8 to bid 74-7/8 and Russian PRIN bonds\tab \tab   were up 1/8 to bid 55-1/4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, on a more sober note, a senior Chinese official on Wednesday issued Beijing's first explicit warning that a sliding Japanese yen could force China to devalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sun Zhenyu, the vice-minister for foreign trade, said a devaluation may be necessary if the tumbling yen hit Chinese exports too hard.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although Washington's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the yen will help the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Devi aurora, Asia analyst at Standard & Poor's DRI, said she expects a devaluation early next year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The worsening outlook for Chinese exports will put great pressure on the yuan," Aurora said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The markets for Chinese goods has declined over the last year due to recessions throughout Asia.\par \f28 