\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ruble Off Lows On Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Rate Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1998\par 19:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble (RUR) ended little changed against the dollar Wednesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tripled its benchmark interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dried up by midday, however, with participants spooked by the volatility of trading. Bond prices plunged, with yields rising to around 90%. \par \par \uc2  Heavy selling forced the ruble out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declared range of trading early in the day, to as low as RUR6.1905 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Late in the day, however, one trader cited one deal with the dollar at RUR6.1740, but said that there was "no market" at that time. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, the dollar for next-day delivery closed at RUR6.1830-6.1850. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it was too early to say whether the rate rise would help the ruble, since trading was so illiquid in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tripled its key discount rate and Lombard lending rates to 150% from 50%. The rate rise followed the collapse of the treasury market Wednesday, when yields on the one-year government bond (GKO) surged to near 90% during an additional secondary market trading session. \par \par \uc2  Normally Wednesdays, the Finance Ministery sells GKOs at the weekly auctions, but this time it decided to allow an hour of additional secondary market trading. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-0