\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ruble Sinks Vs Dlr Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1998\par 18:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Fears of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation drove the ruble lower against the dollar in heavy trading late Monday - its losses only limited by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent at least $500 million to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Selling pressure was likewise heavy in the treasury market, where the benchmark one-year issue rose to 44% from 39.9% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Late in the afternoon, the dollar for next-day delivery changed hands at RUR6.190-6.191, compared with RUR6.180-6.190 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think that it's in the interests of the government to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it seems some people think they will," said a trader at a major western commercial bank in Moscow. "And, if enough people believe it will happen, then it will." \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the forward market in the ruble all but disappeared Monday. Indicative quotes, however, assumed a 40% devaluation of the ruble sometime soon. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were no real developments Monday to spark the latest selling. Panicked by the chaos in Indonesia, and fearing that Russia is the next emerging market to crumble, investors began dumping treasuries last week and resumed doing so at the beginning of trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement last week that it was raising Lombard lending rates apparently did little to stem the tide from the treasury market. On Monday, the rise took effect: the Lombard rate - the rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lends money to commercial banks - rose to 36% for 14-day rates and 40% for 15-day to 30-day rates. The rate had been fixed at at 30%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1638GMT \par \par \uc2  1150 1855 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5i046ps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
