\par\par \b \uc2  Analysts' comments on Russian interest rate moves. \b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1998\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, May 15 (Reuters) - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would leave its key refinancing raise unchanged at 30 percent but would raise the 3-14 day Lombard rate to 36 from 30 percent and the 15-30 day Lombard rate to 40 from 30 percent effective from May 18. \par \par \uc2  Analysts gave the following comments to Reuters and to Reuters television after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement: \par \par \uc2  STEPHEN LEWIS, MONUMENT DERIVATIVES, LONDON: "This is a good strategy as long as it works. If it starts falling apart the risk will be that the economy itself will begin to suffer from inflationary pressures through a weakening in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that will probably force some increase in the refinancing rate as well as in some of the other rates. \par \par \uc2  "International investors, speculators, call them what you will, I think that they do look at risky situations where they suspect that official reserves are not large enough to cover potential outflow on short term capital account and that is one dimension where Russia could be said to bear some similarities to nations that have got themselves into trouble in Asia." \par \par \uc2  "Russian authorities have shown some skill in warding off pressures...They do seem to be getting more expert in dealing with the markets." \par \par \uc2  RICHARD GRAY, BANK OF AMERICA, LONDON: "I think it is a fairly notional move on the Lombard rate. Longer term, though, it might become a bit more interesting in terms of a change of direction in how Russian authorities manage money market instruments in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Just recently they've been using \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the GKO (t-bill) auctions as a primary tool of monetary policy. If they are coming back onto these headline rates, then that's a change of gear, but it could be constructive long term." \par \par \uc2  INNA FRANCIS, UNITED FINANCIAL GROUP, MOSCOW: "The refinancing rate is a key benchmark, and its being kept at the same level is just a sign that they want to show there is nothing really disturbing about the situation in the economy and that the pressures everyone is talking about on the rouble are not that substantial. \par \par \uc2  "But at the same time raising the long-term Lombard rate means that they are trying to prevent arbitrage opportunities... for Russian banks between the rate at which banks borrow money and rate at which the government places GKOs (t-bills) at auction. \par \par \uc2  "There was no outflow of capital so I don't know whether by raising the rate they will attract new money...They are trying to ease pressure on GKO yields but I don't think (just because of the rate raise) the GKO levels will slam down to 22 percent, which is the desirable level according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. Something major has to happen before that happens...like passing the tax code or a rise in oil prices." ((Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941-8520 moscow.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5f0579c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
