\par\par \b \uc2  Chicago/Ruble Futures -2: Liquidity Seen Low At First \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1998\par 15:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  But there are myriad risks associated with trading in any new contract, let alone one that is tied directly to a wobbly emerging market. Liquidity in the ruble futures - which will be non-deliverable, cash-settled contracts sized at 500,000 rubles - will initially be low, meaning investors who decide to own them may find it difficult to locate a buyer. Furthermore, if the future's price plummets, as some analysts predict, the investor could suffer huge losses. \par \par \uc2  Russia's troubled financial sector may not have seen its worst bout of investor fright. The country is plagued with problems, from its ineffective tax system to its massive wage arrears to the likelihood that the slowdown in exports could result in its first trade deficit. Those factors in part precipitated a flight from the Russian bond and stock markets and, in turn, led to the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move last Friday to hike interest rates 14 percentage points to 42%. \par \par \uc2  And that's not all, said Max Tessier, an analyst at Bank Credit Analyst Research Group who has closely followed Russia's markets. Russia has a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that doesn't have a strong mandate from the government, leading to weak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts and an anemic banking system, he added. '\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's market is driven by insider trading, there's a big underground economy, and it's a well-known fact that 'gray' money moves around. All these things add up to much greater risk,' concluded Tessier. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures are commonly used by financial institutions to hedge foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk. But speculators and large hedge funds can also employ the instruments to depress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Market watchers say further market instability in Russia could prompt corporations to dump rubles for a safe-harbor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opening the ruble to speculative attacks. At a basic level, a reenactment of Southeast Asia's crisis. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-02-98 \par \par \uc2  1425GMT \par \par \uc2  1131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du260112s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
