\par\par \b \uc2  Russian Ruble Strengthens Vs. Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par 18:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruble strengthened against the dollar Thursday, boosted by an ongoing shortage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  Traders were loath to name a single reason for the rise, which came late in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Some said the government, which has been taking pains to pay pensions and wages in the regions, had soaked up most of the supply of Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Others said demand for treasuries, which was strong at the treasury auctions Wednesday, was also a factor. The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been guiding the ruble slowly lower against the dollar, was forced to sell rubles late in the session. \par \par \uc2  Late in the afternoon, the dollar for next-day delivery changed hands at 5744-5745 rubles, up from 5753-5754 rubles the day before. \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the official rate for the dollar at 5753 rubles Thursday, up from 5752 rubles on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1634GMT \par \par \uc2  1150 1855 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4h02m3z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
