\par\par \b \uc2  Russian Ruble Gains Vs. Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buying Cited \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1996\par 15:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble gained some ground against the dollar Monday, pushed higher by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the dollar was quoted at 4863-66 rubles for next-day delivery, down from 4868-71 rubles Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said demand for the dollar was strong among commercial banks Monday as investors continued to unload treasury bills, coverting the proceeds into dollars amid growing pre-election uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  At the late-morning fixing on the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICE), Russia's largest, the dollar jumped 12 points to 4860 rubles. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $55 million of the $128 million in turnover to slow the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on the interbank market after the fixing pulled dollar quotes there lower, dealers said, soaking up demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday was a clear sign the bank remains committed to its policy of gradually guiding the ruble lower, keeping the depreciation rate below inflation, however. \par \par \uc2  Reports Monday that the government plans to declare this policy officially after the current target corridor expires June 30 had little effect on the market, dealers said, since the move would reflect no real change in policy. \par \par \uc2  For the rest of the week, participants said, the dollar is expected to return to its slow uptrend, gaining a few rubles a day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-05-96 \par \par \uc2  1342GMT \par \par \uc2  1150 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5603qo7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
