\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Calms  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Mkts, But Risks Seen: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By GREG WHITE and ALAN CULLISON \par \uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1995\par 17:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (AP-DJ)--Russian authorities pumped more than a trillion rubles in emergency funds into the financial markets Friday, easing a liquidity crisis that had paralyzed trading on the country's young markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government succeeded in calming the panic, and \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all sectors - \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interbank loans and treasuries - were sputtering to life by late in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'They took the edge off the situation,' said Kirill Borisov, senior treasury analyst at Bank Menatep. \par \par \uc2  But bankers and government officials warned that the markets could take weeks to fully recover. \par \par \uc2  In addition, Russia's still fragile banking system could face more shakeout as trading margins shrink and bad debts mount. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, repeated bailouts, flooding the economy with excess rubles, could defeat the government's attempts to stabilize the economy, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Government officials played down the latest tension, assuring the public the situation was well under control. \par \par \uc2  'What happened yesterday (Thursday) on the interbank market, in our opinion, was a short-term surge in illiquidity among Moscow banks,' First Deputy Prime Minister Anatoly Chubais told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  'By the middle of (Friday) the situation was resolved. Banks have sufficient funds,' he added. \par \par \uc2  After buying 600 billion rubles in treasury bills Thursday - about 40% of all trading volume - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought another trillion Friday, bank officials said. Settlement rules were changed to give banks the rubles from those trades Friday, instead of Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-08-95 \par \par \uc2  1513GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8p06iq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
