\par\par \b \uc2  Russia/High Inflation -3: Russians Shifting Back To Rubles \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 1995\par 18:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'What is really important is how much money is growing compared to how much the population wants it to grow,' he says. \par \par \uc2  Layard of the London School of Economics agrees that Russians are shifting their portfolios, unloading part of the estimated $20 billion in dollar holdings built up in recent years. But he concedes that the data don't yet back this up. \par \par \uc2  If the ruble really had become the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice, he notes, people would be more willing to hold onto money, since inflation no longer threatened its value on a daily basis. As a result, rubles would circulate more slowly through the economy. \par \par \uc2  So far, however, this velocity remains high - about twice the level seen in much of Eastern Europe, for example - and isn't showing signs of falling, Layard concedes. \par \par \uc2  'We'll only be able to see later whether there has been a permanent increase in the demand for rubles,' he says. \par \par \uc2  In the interim, economists warn, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is running a risk by pumping the economy with new rubles. \par \par \uc2  'Monetary growth must be restrained from now on,' says Layard. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has substantially slowed dollar buying in recent months, and the corridor set for the ruble July 6 has added to stability in the market. But, analysts say, mechanisms such as open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that central banks in other countries routinely use to clean up excess money created by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in their infancy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As a result, economists say, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could find many of the rubles it printed this spring back on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this fall if stabilization doesn't show results in the form of sharply lower inflation. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-07-95 \par \par \uc2  1639GMT \par \par \uc2  1144 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7h05e29\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
