\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Central Banker:  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fueling Inflation \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 1995\par 17:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (AP-DJ)--Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rise in the ruble in recent months has bloated the money supply and fueled inflation, the ITAR-Tass news agency quoted Tatyana Paramonova, acting chairwoman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia, as saying Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'We're forced to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies and individuals and as a result release more and more new money, which supports the inflationary process,' Tass quoted her as telling reporters at a banking congress in St. Petersburg. \par \par \uc2  The ruble has gained 4% against the dollar since the beginning of May and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stem the rise. In Moscow Wednesday, the dollar rebounded slightly, gaining 6 points to 4906 rubles. \par \par \uc2  Paramonova said that if it weren't for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , monthly inflation would be below the current 7%-8% rate. In May, consumer prices rose 7.9%, above government targets of 5%-6%. \par \par \uc2  In the past, the central banker has noted that money-supply growth caused by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't as inflationary as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lending to finance the budget deficit, the main source of inflation in Russia in recent years. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-06-95 \par \par \uc2  1518GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr67048nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi