\par\par \b \uc2  Russian Ruble Continues Lower Vs. Dlr, But Shortage Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1995\par 14:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (AP-DJ)--The ruble continued lower against the dollar Friday, but traders said the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in short supply and attributed the slide to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICE), \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest, the dollar was fixed at 4191.0 rubles Friday, up from 4170.0 rubles Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Off the exchange, the dollar was quoted about 25 points below the MICE fixing level, reflecting slack demand, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But on the exchange, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took advantage of the situation and bought dollars to keep the market on track. The bank has committed itself to keeping the ruble sliding roughly in line with inflation. \par \par \uc2  Investors, meanwhile, were shifting money back and forth from the exchange to the interbank market to capitalize on the spread, traders said, with no longer-term trends to latch onto. \par \par \uc2  Volume on the exchange was light at 79 million dlrs Friday, down from 102 million dlrs Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Participants said the ruble shortage is likely to continue early next week ahead of Wednesday's record 2.8-trillion-ruble treasury bill offering. T-bills are among the highest-yielding instruments in the money market at the moment, and demand at recent auctions has been strong. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep the dollar steady if not rising against the ruble next week, building its reserves. \par \par \uc2  This week, the dollar gained 1.8% against the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-02-95 \par \par \uc2  1313GMT \par \par \uc2  1150 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2a00um8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
